Expanded Delight, unofficial modified build for Forge 1.20.1
============================================================

This is an UNOFFICIAL, MODIFIED build of Expanded Delight. Its author does not
support it. Report problems with it at
https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server/issues, not upstream.

Original work
-------------
  Expanded Delight by ianm1647
  Source:  https://github.com/ianm1647/expandeddelight
  Content: branch 1.21-neo @ ea826400654702587e86c9e94544bfd74f065083
           (2026-08-25, Expanded Delight 0.1.4 for NeoForge 1.21.1)
  API reference for Minecraft 1.20.1: branch 1.20 @ 8d8fe44d9b4cba54c47f84c5836872a803388cb2
           (2026-01-14, Expanded Delight 0.4.0 for Fabric 1.20.1)

Modifications
-------------
  Modified by SkyTekx in 2026 for the SkyTekx 3 modpack. The build runs on
  Minecraft 1.20.1 with Forge 47, keeps the mod id expandeddelight and is versioned
  0.1.4-skytekx.1.

  - The content of 0.1.4 is ported from the NeoForge 1.21.1 API to Forge 1.20.1:
    data components became item stack NBT, NeoForge capabilities and events became
    Forge capabilities and events, and the data files use the 1.20.1 folder names,
    formats and forge: tags.
  - Bugs of 0.1.4 that this build fixes and the parts it leaves out are listed in
    UPSTREAM.md in the source directory.

  Source: the directory ports/expandeddelight of
    https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server
  The exact source of a given jar is that directory at the commit that added the
  jar to local-mods/.

Upstream files left out and replaced
------------------------------------
  The 1.21-neo branch contains material of Farmer's Respite, which is All Rights
  Reserved on CurseForge and Modrinth and has no public source. This build leaves
  it out:
  - textures/gui/juicer.png and textures/gui/jei/juicer.png, a juicer GUI sheet
    built on the kettle sheet of Farmer's Respite. The juicer screen uses the
    author's own textures/gui/juicer_gui.png of the 1.20 branch (commit
    50e9c102aaa44dedae924ee1dc381af17aaa3d69, 2022) instead.
  - textures/item/empty_container_slot_bottle.png, a byte copy of a Farmer's
    Respite icon. The bottle slot needs no icon, the 1.20 sheet draws one.
  - common/block/entity/container/JuicerMenu.java, decompiled from the KettleMenu
    of Farmer's Respite. This build has a new JuicerMenu, written from the
    CookingPotMenu of Farmer's Delight (MIT) with slot positions that match the
    1.20 sheet.
  It also leaves out three unused textures that copy other work: the vanilla
  item/glass_bottle.png and item/sweet_berries.png, and block/rice_bag_bottom.png
  of Farmer's Delight.

